{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EzUwYum4vVxAHCacV5WtGU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-579\"\n3\ttitle = \"The verdict carrier and the adjudication_review dial: gate over logged rounds, tree-bound trailer, generated rollup\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n7\tpriority = 9\n8\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n9\tsupersedes = \"WI-558;WI-559;WI-560\"\n10\t+++\n11\t\n12\t## Deliverable\n13\t\n14\tThe merge gate reads the EVIDENCE and the evidence names the tree it judged.\n15\t\n16\t`kitlib/verdict.py` (LLR-207, IF-175) is the verdict record's one home: the\n17\tnon-record tree identity — a SHA-256 fold of `git ls-tree -r -z` with\n18\t`docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/` and `docs/iteration/` dropped — the\n19\t`Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>` trailer\n20\tgrammar, the round-file / session-log join, and the branch-scoped readers. Two\n21\tcallers stand on it and that is the point: `integrate._verdict_gate` (may this\n22\tmerge?) and `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` (does this lane still owe a\n23\tround?) asked one question with two rules over two exclusion sets, and the gap\n24\tbetween them drew two identical rounds on WI-547.\n25\t\n26\t- **WI-558 DW1** — the gate computes over the branch's own round files,\n27\t  restricted to rounds a LOGGED reviewer session produced: a file under\n28\t  `docs/reviews/` is a round only when the coordinator's own committed session\n29\t  log for that (train, ordinal) declares a REVIEW phase. Finding K closed —\n30\t  an implementer cannot author its own approval without also forging the loop's\n31\t  telemetry.\n32\t- **WI-558 DW2** — the machine half rides the round's own record commit as a\n33\t  trailer, written by the COORDINATOR and verified against its carrier's tree\n34\t  (the `Bar-Green` pattern). GOVERNING = TREE IDENTITY: a verdict counts only\n35\t  while it names the branch's current non-record tree, read at the WORK TIP so\n36\t  the station refresh still does not stale an honest APPROVE. The freshness\n37\t  comparison is gone; there is no ordering rule left. The trailer is a\n38\t  CROSS-CHECK and never an accept path — one that contradicts the rounds\n39\t  refuses the merge.\n40\t- **WI-558 DW3** — `gen_verdict_rollup.py` (LLR-208) rebirths the rollup as a\n41\t  GENERATED artifact: `docs/stack.ini [generated]`, `trunk_step.py --regen`, a\n42\t  `check.py verdict-rollup` freshness step on the hook floor and in\n43\t  `_TRUNK_FRESHNESS_STEPS`, and `--check` with two answers. The gate never reads\n44\t  it, and the file says so where a human will see it.\n45\t- **WI-558 DW4** — the migration window: the gate accepts EITHER the round\n46\t  evidence or a legacy hand-authored rollup, judged by the SAME identity rule,\n47\t  warning on stderr whenever the legacy path is what cleared it. Two\n48\t  `RESYNC_PACK.md` entries. The trailer is additive and costs an adopter nothing.\n49\t- **WI-558 DW5 / WI-560 DW4 / WI-559 DW3** — `tests/test_verdict_record.py`\n50\t  drives each half beside its opposite (TC-205, TC-206).\n51\t- **WI-560 DW1** — ONE definition of \"the last commit that could invalidate a\n52\t  verdict\", used by the merge slot AND the C2 review-owed derivation. That\n53\t  definition names a REV as well as a path set, so the station-refresh peel\n54\t  (`refresh_attestation` / `work_tip`) lives beside the fold and both readers\n55\t  call `governing_identity` rather than each choosing where to measure. The\n56\t  double-identical-round class is now unrepresentable, not policed: the commits\n57\t  that caused it cannot move the identity either reader compares.\n58\t- **WI-559 DW2** — a committing ADJUDICATE session schedules its round exactly\n59\t  as a committing BUILD does, under the dial; the phase stays in\n60\t  `NON_BUILD_PHASES` because a judgement is not a build. No exit banner claims a\n61\t  round that was never drawn — it counts them.\n62\t- **The dial** — `docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review`\n63\t  (`never` / `when-minting` / `always`; template and this repo ship\n64\t  `when-minting`), read through `agent_common.adjudication_review_owed` by BOTH\n65\t  the scheduler and the gate, with a closed vocabulary refused at preflight and\n66\t  a conservative fallback. Its `docs/enforcement-audit.md` row and the\n67\t  `RESYNC_PACK.md` entry ship with it. An adjudication lane drafting ordinary\n68\t  successors now merges with NO verdict artifact present anywhere — the OI-76\n69\t  acceptance becomes measurable on the next unattended run.\n70\t\n71\tReview A rework closed both evidence-boundary gaps. The loop's resume reader now\n72\tuses the same branch-scoped committed-path, logged-session and tree-bound entry\n73\tpipeline as the merge gate, so an approval-shaped file produced by a BUILD\n74\tsession cannot suppress the round the gate requires. The trailer's `rounds=N`\n75\tfield is now defined and checked as the completed review cycles represented at\n76\tthe governing tree (a dual-review cycle counts once, and rework starts the\n77\ttree-scoped count over); both the coordinator writer and gate derive that value\n78\tfrom the shared evidence. LLR-207's rationale now carries only the standing\n79\ttechnical reason, without the decision's provenance narrative.\n80\t\n81\tReview A round 007 closed four more, three of them one shape — a rule expressed\n82\tas a value something else got to choose. The identity's REV is now part of the\n83\tshared definition (the peel moved into `kitlib/verdict.py`, so a station refresh\n84\tno longer makes the two readers disagree); `branch_trailers` returns the ordered\n85\tSEQUENCE of attestations per tree, so the newest-first `git log` can no longer\n86\thand a reader a superseded stamp and have the cross-check accuse an approved\n87\tlane of forgery; and `tree_identity` passes `-z` while `fold_listing` takes\n88\tdecoded entries, so a quoted non-ASCII path can no longer fold a record file\n89\tinto the identity. The DONE banner states rounds DRAWN this run and the latest\n90\tverdict, because the tally it reads holds every completed round whatever its\n91\toutcome.\n92\t\n93\tVerifying finding 2's fix end-to-end found a fifth defect of the same family,\n94\tdriven and closed here. The refresh peel was TIP-ONLY, because `work_tip` is\n95\tshared with the `reset --hard` in `integrate.refresh` where peeling one commit\n96\ttoo far destroys work. So a telemetry commit — a `docs/iteration/` record path,\n97\twhich the fold exists to ignore — moved the governing identity anyway, by\n98\tBURYING the refresh under it: the loop answered `owed=True` and the merge slot\n99\trefused \"no logged review round names its current tree\", both readers agreeing\n100\ton the wrong answer and parking an honest APPROVE at a supervisor stop. That is\n101\tthe OI-76 failure mode itself, one commit further down than round 007 reached.\n102\t`governing_rev` now walks through record-only commits to reach the refresh, and\n103\t`work_tip` keeps its tip-only contract untouched — the two shapes of the peel\n104\tare separate because a read-only reader can afford an answer a destructive one\n105\tcannot.\n106\t\n107\t`LLR-140`'s Approved detail cell was re-pointed IN-LANE: it asserted the retired\n108\ttime comparison, which nothing detects once it is false. Ratchet bumps\n109\t(`agent_common` 1272→1305, `agent_loop` 2519→2578, `integrate` 1298→1382 and\n110\tthen DOWN to 1352 when the peel left it, `check` 1163→1177, `bootstrap`\n111\t1658→1660, smoke membership 1480→1560) each carry\n112\ttheir reason at the entry; `_verdict_gate`'s complexity bump was REFUSED and the\n113\tfunction decomposed instead. Round-007 rework full suite, run at the tip\n114\t`cee19210`: 3343 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed in 615.27s — the failure is\n115\t`docs/stage` freshness, a trunk-lane artifact a work branch must\n116\tnot commit, bisected clean at the integration base. Account, deviations and the\n117\tone out-of-scope finding: `docs/log.d/WI-579-verdict-carrier-and-adjudication-review.md`.\n118\t\n119\t## Context\n120\t\n121\tMinted by the owner-directed backlog restructure of 2026-09-02 (plan of record `docs/plans/2026-09-02-backlog-restructure-and-consolidation.md` §2.2; executed out of band as a hand trunk commit series, not by a lane). The absorbed rows are archived under `docs/archive/work/restructured/` with their scope text untouched; their Done-when blocks are QUOTED below under their old ids and remain the spec this row must satisfy — decompose, don't paraphrase.\n122\t\n123\t**Why one row.** WI-558 Done-when 2 retires the gate's freshness comparison in\n124\tfavour of tree identity; WI-560 Done-when 1 builds one shared freshness\n125\tdefinition for the gate and the C2 review-owed derivation; WI-559 Done-when 2\n126\tmakes an ADJUDICATE commit schedule a round, which only means something once\n127\tthe round carrier WI-558 defines exists. Built apart in any order, the later\n128\tlane undoes part of the earlier one. Together: the gate and the review-owed\n129\tderivation read the SAME tree-identity trailer, and the round an adjudication\n130\towes is drawn under the policy below.\n131\t\n132\t**Adjudication review policy (plan §3, owner direction 2026-09-02).** The\n133\tadjudicator is already the cross-family judge by routing (`agent_loop`'s\n134\tADJUDICATE arm excludes the builder's family). A round over every adjudication\n135\tis a fresh session with less context judging the one session that held the\n136\twhole chain, and today it is also the supervisor stop on every unattended run\n137\t(`integrate._verdict_gate` demands a REVIEW-A from a lane whose phase is in\n138\t`NON_BUILD_PHASES`, so nothing produces one). This row adds\n139\t`docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review = \"never\" | \"when-minting\" | \"always\"`\n140\t(template ships `\"when-minting\"`, this repo sets `\"when-minting\"`):\n141\t- `never` — no round after ADJUDICATE; the gate never asks an adjudication\n142\t  lane for a verdict.\n143\t- `when-minting` — a round is scheduled, and the gate demands its verdict,\n144\t  when the merged adjudication's `## Dispositions` drafts ANY successor whose\n145\t  `safety_class` is `spine` or `high-risk`, or when its `brief` is\n146\t  `consolidate`. An amendment verdict that only recommends a flip, a red-tc\n147\t  that drafts ordinary fix rows, a clean-close spot check: no round.\n148\t- `always` — the intended-but-broken behaviour today, made real.\n149\tOne reader function in `agent_common` (`adjudication_review_owed(docs, brief,\n150\tdrafts)`) serves BOTH the round scheduler (ADJUDICATE leaves the unconditional\n151\t`NON_BUILD_PHASES` set; the dial decides) and `_verdict_gate` (which consults\n152\tthe existing `integrate._adjudication_lane` plus the dial plus the merged\n153\tspec's drafts), so the two cannot disagree. Tests pin all three values on a\n154\tscaffold and pin that `never`/`when-minting` with ordinary drafts lets an\n155\tadjudication lane merge with NO REVIEW-A file present.\n156\t\n157\t## Done-when\n158\t\n159\t1. Every WI-558 Done-when item below, as written.\n160\t2. WI-560 Done-when 1 below, satisfied by the SAME trailer/tree-identity rule\n161\t   the gate uses (one definition, two readers).\n162\t3. WI-559 Done-when 2 below, under the `adjudication_review` dial.\n163\t4. The dial, its template row, `docs/enforcement-audit.md` row, and the\n164\t   `RESYNC_PACK.md` entry.\n165\t5. Full suite green; the OI-76 acceptance (three consecutive rows merged by\n166\t   one launch with zero supervisor commits) is measurable on the next\n167\t   unattended run.\n168\t\n169\t### From WI-558 (Done-when, verbatim)\n170\t\n171\t1. `integrate._verdict_gate` computes its predicate over the branch train's\n172\t   round files, restricted to rounds a LOGGED reviewer session produced (the\n173\t   telemetry commit is the anchor) — an implementer-authored file in the\n174\t   review path is not a round (the plan's finding K closed).\n175\t2. The round's own commit carries the machine half as a trailer —\n176\t   `Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=N tree=<sha>` — the\n177\t   existing `Bar-Green` pattern. GOVERNING = TREE IDENTITY as ruled: a\n178\t   verdict counts only if it names the branch's current non-record tree; no\n179\t   ordering rule; the gate's freshness comparison retires.\n180\t3. The per-WI rollup becomes a GENERATED artifact: a regenerator compiles it\n181\t   from the round files, `--check` keeps it fresh, it is declared in\n182\t   `docs/stack.ini [generated]`, and the gate never reads it. The supervisor\n183\t   prompt's hand-compile instruction retires in the same change.\n184\t4. Migration window per the plan's section 6: during the window the gate\n185\t   accepts EITHER the round-file evidence or a legacy hand-authored rollup,\n186\t   warning on the legacy path; `RESYNC_PACK.md` carries the entry. The\n187\t   trailer is additive and costs an adopter nothing until their loop writes\n188\t   one.\n189\t5. Tests drive the gate's new predicate, the trailer identity rule, the\n190\t   logged-session restriction, and the migration warn on a scaffold; the\n191\t   full suite stays green.\n192\t\n193\t### From WI-560 (Done-when 1 and 4, verbatim — 2 went to WI-580, 3 to WI-581; item 4 is shared)\n194\t\n195\t1. ONE shared definition of \"the last commit that could invalidate a\n196\t   verdict\" (excluding `docs/reviews`, `docs/log.d`, `docs/iteration`) is\n197\t   used by both the merge slot and the C2 review-owed derivation; the\n198\t   double-identical-round class becomes unrepresentable on a scaffold.\n199\t4. Tests drive all three.\n200\t\n201\t### From WI-559 (Done-when 2 and 3, verbatim — Done-when 1 went to WI-580; item 3 is shared with it)\n202\t\n203\t2. A committing ADJUDICATE session schedules its review round exactly as a\n204\t   committing BUILD 
